  "narrative": {
    "northStar":"A living geometry index",
    "overview":"A botanical learning index contributes pine ink, pale leaf, paper and compact specimen previews. Familiar application controls carry the task. The actual turtle geometry is the signature: previews are executed programs, and the primary canvas is always the work itself.",
    "keyCharacteristics":["Code and geometric consequence share the workspace.","Pine and leaf carry navigation and execution state.","Linework is exact output, never illustrative decoration.","Flat surfaces, fine rules and compact controls."],
    "rules":[{"name":"The True Geometry Rule","body":"Interface themes never recolor a user's drawing.","section":"colors"}],
    "dos":["Do use actual interpreted geometry for previews.","Do keep errors positioned and written in Polish.","Do preserve independent drafts and make recovery visible.","Do retain the same navigation and controls across viewport sizes."],
    "donts":["Don't recolor drawing segments to match a theme.","Don't simulate botanical materials or add decorative specimens.","Don't use monospace for general interface prose."]
